<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<title>predval report -- {{ cohort_id }}</title>
<style>
 body { font: 15px/1.5 -apple-system, system-ui, sans-serif; max-width: 60rem; margin: 2rem auto;
        padding: 0 1rem; color: #1a1a1a; }
 h1 { font-size: 1.6rem; } h2 { font-size: 1.2rem; margin-top: 2.2rem;
        border-bottom: 1px solid #ddd; padding-bottom: .3rem; }
 table { border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: .6rem 0; font-size: .92rem; }
 th, td { text-align: left; padding: .35rem .6rem; border-bottom: 1px solid #eee; }
 th { background: #f6f6f6; }
 .framing { background: #fff8e6; border: 2px solid #e0b400; border-radius: 6px;
        padding: 1rem 1.2rem; margin: 1rem 0 1.5rem; font-weight: 500; }
 .subordinate { color: #333; font-size: .9rem; }
 .muted { color: #666; } .warn { color: #b00; } code { font-size: .85em; }
 .byconstruction { font-style: italic; color: #666; }
 .figure { margin: 1rem 0; }
 .figure svg { max-width: 100%; height: auto; }
 .limitations { background: #f4f6f8; border-left: 3px solid #123B5E; padding: .8rem 1rem;
        margin: 1.2rem 0; font-size: .92rem; }
 .appendix { margin-top: 2.5rem; border-top: 2px solid #ddd; padding-top: 1rem; }
 @media print {
   /* The pitch path is browser print-to-PDF; there is no PDF pipeline. Keep it clean on paper. */
   body { max-width: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; font-size: 10.5pt; color: #000; }
   a { color: #000; text-decoration: none; }
   h2 { page-break-after: avoid; }
   table, tr, .framing { page-break-inside: avoid; }
   /* Keep the framing box and header shading visible on paper, not dropped as "backgrounds". */
   .framing { -webkit-print-color-adjust: exact; print-color-adjust: exact; }
   th { -webkit-print-color-adjust: exact; print-color-adjust: exact; }
 }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<h1>predval report</h1>
<p class="muted">cohort: <code>{{ cohort_id }}</code></p>

<div class="framing">{{ framing }}</div>

<h2>1. Coverage and roster</h2>
{% if roster.declared is not none %}
<p>Roster: <strong>{{ roster.declared }}</strong> declared,
   <strong>{{ roster.present }}</strong> present,
   <strong>{{ roster.absent | length }}</strong> absent{% if roster.absent %}
   (<span class="warn">{{ roster.absent | join(", ") }}</span> -- declared but no predictions){% endif %}.</p>
{% else %}
<p class="muted">No model roster was declared.</p>
{% endif %}
<table>
<tr><th>model</th><th>coverage</th><th>scored</th><th>dropped if common</th><th>meets minimum</th></tr>
{% for r in coverage_rows %}
<tr><td>{{ r.model }}</td><td>{{ r.coverage_full }}</td><td>{{ r.n_scored }}</td>
    <td>{{ r.n_dropped_if_common }}</td>
    <td>{% if r.meets_minimum %}yes{% else %}<span class="warn">no</span>{% endif %}</td></tr>
{% endfor %}
</table>

<h2>2. Primary comparison -- model as published (rung0)</h2>
<p class="muted">Common subset, overall stratum. AUROC and Brier carry cluster intervals; the
calibration slope and intercept carry cluster-robust analytic intervals.
{% if identical_coverage %}Full and common coverage are identical here, so the coverage-delta
column is omitted (every value would be zero).{% else %}The final column is AUROC full minus
common -- the effect of restricting to the common subset.{% endif %}</p>
<table>
<tr><th>model</th><th>AUROC</th><th>avg precision</th><th>Brier</th><th>calib slope</th>
    <th>calib intercept</th>{% if not identical_coverage %}<th>AUROC cov-delta</th>{% endif %}</tr>
{% for r in primary_rows %}
<tr><td>{{ r.model }}</td><td>{{ r.auroc }}</td><td>{{ r.average_precision }}</td>
    <td>{{ r.brier }}</td><td>{{ r.calibration_slope }}</td><td>{{ r.calibration_intercept }}</td>
    {% if not identical_coverage %}<td>{{ r.cov_delta }}</td>{% endif %}</tr>
{% endfor %}
</table>
{% if brier_footnote %}
<p class="muted">Brier intervals above are the cluster percentile bootstrap (a non-negative loss
cannot cross 0). The analytic t(G-1) cross-check is in metrics.parquet; being symmetric it can fall
below the 0 loss boundary, and is truncated at 0 where it did:
{% for r in brier_footnote %}{{ r.model }} {{ r.interval }} (raw lower {{ r.raw_low }}){% if not loop.last %}; {% endif %}{% endfor %}.
Where truncated, <em>{{ analytic_truncated_note }}</em>.</p>
{% else %}
<p class="muted">Brier intervals above are the cluster percentile bootstrap; the analytic t(G-1)
cross-check in metrics.parquet agrees (none crossed the 0 loss boundary).</p>
{% endif %}

{% if verdict_lines %}
<h3>Verdict</h3>
<p class="muted">One line per member, assembled only from AUROC, the Brier skill score (BSS), and the
best admissible rung -- no free adjectives. BSS is anchored at <strong>0 = no-skill</strong> (always
predict prevalence) and <strong>1 = perfect</strong>; "closes Y% of the gap" is BSS as a percentage.
The gauge sentence states any detected miscalibration (slope or intercept interval excluding its
null), the lowest rung whose out-of-fold repair is demonstrated, and any rung whose recalibration
reliably harms. A member with no detected fault and no demonstrated repair carries no gauge
sentence: the test can fail to reject calibration but never establish it.</p>
<ul>
{% for v in verdict_lines %}
<li><strong>{{ v.model }}</strong> -- {{ v.line }}</li>
{% endfor %}
</ul>
{% endif %}

{% if calibration_svg %}
<h3>Calibration (rung0, as published)</h3>
<p class="muted">Decile calibration per member: points are observed frequency against mean predicted
probability, the shaded band is the cluster bootstrap on the observed rate, and the dashed diagonal
is <em>perfect</em>. Points below the diagonal over-predict risk; above, under-predict.</p>
<div class="figure">{{ calibration_svg | safe }}</div>
{% endif %}

{% if exhibit_rows %}
<h3>Unit-of-analysis exhibit</h3>
<p class="muted">{{ exhibit_note | safe }}</p>
<table>
<tr><th>model</th><th>cluster width</th><th>naive width (wrong)</th><th>ratio</th></tr>
{% for r in exhibit_rows %}
<tr><td>{{ r.model }}</td><td>{{ r.cluster_width }}</td><td>{{ r.naive_width }}</td>
    <td>{{ r.ratio }}</td></tr>
{% endfor %}
</table>
{% if dumbbell_svg %}<div class="figure">{{ dumbbell_svg | safe }}</div>{% endif %}
{% endif %}

<h2>3. Calibration diagnosis (subordinate to section 2)</h2>
<p class="subordinate">This section diagnoses rung0; it does not rank models. Rows are ordered with
demonstrated repairs first (by rung, then by interval strength), then the remaining members by
their best gain estimate -- the largest point estimate is not the strongest evidence. Each cell is the <strong>paired cross-fit Brier gain</strong> -- rung0 Brier
minus that rung's held-out Brier, positive when recalibration helped -- with its paired
cluster-bootstrap interval (a gain whose interval excludes 0 is a real out-of-fold improvement).
The apparent, in-sample gains run larger; only the cross-fitted gains, which hold whole
{{ cluster_nouns }} out, are shown. rung1's apparent intercept is ~0 and rung2's apparent slope is
~1 <span class="byconstruction">by construction</span> (that is what each fit targets), so those are
not reported as findings. Recalibration cannot improve discrimination; the cross-fitted Brier is the
expected loss after local recalibration, not a validated result.</p>
<p class="subordinate">At small G the flexible rung is high-variance under cross-fitting: absence of
a rung3 gain is evidence of linear miscalibration only insofar as rung3 had power to detect shape
distortion.{% if rung3_diagnosis_doc %} See the fold4 diagnosis
({{ rung3_diagnosis_doc }}) for the members whose rung3 could not be cross-fit on this
cohort.{% endif %}</p>
<table>
<tr><th>model</th><th>Brier rung0</th><th>rung1 gain [CI] (x10⁻³)</th><th>rung2 gain [CI] (x10⁻³)</th>
    <th>rung3 gain [CI] (x10⁻³)</th></tr>
{% for r in calibration_rows %}
<tr><td>{{ r.model }}</td><td>{{ r.rung0 }}</td><td>{{ r.rung1_gain }}</td>
    <td>{{ r.rung2_gain }}</td><td>{{ r.rung3_gain }}</td></tr>
{% endfor %}
</table>
{% if brier_rung_svg %}<div class="figure">{{ brier_rung_svg | safe }}</div>{% endif %}

<h2>4. Subgroups</h2>
{% if subgroup_rows %}
<table>
<tr><th>subgroup</th><th>model</th><th>AUROC</th><th>Brier</th></tr>
{% for r in subgroup_rows %}
<tr><td>{{ r.subgroup }}</td><td>{{ r.model }}</td><td>{{ r.auroc }}</td><td>{{ r.brier }}</td></tr>
{% endfor %}
</table>
{% else %}
<p class="muted">No subgroups were prespecified.</p>
{% endif %}
{% for f in flags.note if f.code == "recalibration_suppressed" %}
{% if loop.first %}<p class="muted">Ladder suppressed on gated subgroups:</p><ul class="muted">{% endif %}
<li>{{ f.message }}</li>
{% if loop.last %}</ul>{% endif %}
{% endfor %}

<h2>5. Fragility -- not a confidence interval</h2>
<p class="muted">The largest AUROC change from dropping any single cluster, and the culprit. This is
deliberately <strong>not</strong> an interval: it answers whether a result is carried by one
{{ cluster_noun }}, which a tight bootstrap interval will not reveal.</p>
{% if fragility_rows %}
<table>
<tr><th>model</th><th>max |delta AUROC|</th><th>culprit cluster</th></tr>
{% for r in fragility_rows %}
<tr><td>{{ r.model }}</td><td>{{ r.max_abs_delta }}</td><td>{{ r.culprit }}</td></tr>
{% endfor %}
</table>
{% else %}
<p class="muted">No fragility rows (fewer than two clusters).</p>
{% endif %}

<h3>Limitations</h3>
<div class="limitations">{{ limitations }}</div>

<h2>6. Provenance</h2>
<p class="muted">Input digests (blake2b), the bootstrap seed and B, and library versions -- enough to
reproduce every number.</p>
<table>
{% for name, digest in provenance.inputs %}
<tr><th>{{ name }}</th><td><code>{{ digest }}</code></td></tr>
{% endfor %}
<tr><th>contract version</th><td>{{ provenance.contract_version }}</td></tr>
<tr><th>bootstrap</th><td>B={{ provenance.uncertainty.n_boot }}, seed={{ provenance.uncertainty.seed }},
    ci={{ provenance.uncertainty.ci_level }}</td></tr>
{% for name, ver in provenance.versions %}
<tr><th>{{ name }}</th><td>{{ ver }}</td></tr>
{% endfor %}
</table>

<h3>Flags</h3>
{% if flags.warning %}
<ul>{% for f in flags.warning %}<li class="warn"><strong>{{ f.code }}</strong>: {{ f.message }}</li>{% endfor %}</ul>
{% endif %}
{% if flags.note %}
<ul class="muted">{% for f in flags.note %}<li><strong>{{ f.code }}</strong>: {{ f.message }}</li>{% endfor %}</ul>
{% endif %}
{% if not flags.warning and not flags.note %}<p class="muted">No flags.</p>{% endif %}

{% if appendix %}
<div class="appendix">
<h2>Appendix -- concepts</h2>
<p class="muted">An optional explainer, off by default. Static SVG assets will be inserted into these
placeholders in a later revision; the structure is fixed now so the default report bytes never carry
it.</p>
{% for title, body in appendix_sections %}
<h3>{{ title }}</h3>
<p class="muted">{{ body }}</p>
{% endfor %}
</div>
{% endif %}

</body>
</html>
